_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:628:2. **OPEN-2 — Identifier alphabet/case (0).** Recommend ASCII `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`, case-sensitive; no casing-based category. Alternative: Unicode XID with a specified normalization policy. Reason: ASCII is auditable and matches old EBNF; OD152 still governs declaration-based resolution.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:630:4. **OPEN-4 — Reserved declaration/builtin inventory (by slice).** Recommend one explicit closed table of every admitted builtin type, grant type, primitive and function, with compiler prefixes and collision scopes; emit no aliases. Alternative: reserve only a compiler namespace and qualify builtin calls. Reason: OD43/133/153 require a publishable complete set; the present materials do not enumerate the final branded/secret/grant surface in one place. This approves an inventory, not unseen APIs. Q7.10 already approves the hosted grant table; only consolidation/transcription is outstanding there.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:637:11. **OPEN-11 — Imports (17).** Recommend `import a.b.{x, y as z};`, nonempty list, mandatory commas, optional trailing comma after factoring; wildcard already refused by [MOD-2](../legacy/docs/spec/modules.md#MOD-2), no whole-module alias or alternate missing-dot form. Alternative: `import a.b {x, y as z};`. Reason: old parser accepts both final-dot styles, so the owner should choose one canonical form.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:640:14. **OPEN-14 — Generic/type grammar closure (11/15/19/20).** Recommend nonempty comma lists, type parameters before cap parameters, type/brand arguments before capability arguments, `cap C`, `+` name unions and `{}` empty set, `[T; INT]`, generic cast targets parenthesized; parse named arguments once then check kind. Alternative: explicit kind-tagged arguments and semicolon-separated capability arguments. Reason: respect OD88/Q5 without pretending IDENT types and sets have disjoint FIRST sets. Approve qualified names, composite cast targets, array length expressions and union spelling inside with individually.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:642:16. **OPEN-16 — Blocks and LL(1) statement/value modes (3/10/20).** Recommend retain decided statement/value behavior, explicit function returns, no standalone block primary, and derive one common-prefix block grammar with delayed control-node classification as described in section 4. Alternative: require explicit grouping of tail if/match or a tail marker, **only after checking and explicitly revising any decided acceptance it changes**. Reason: a position-blind grammar with both `{stmt}` and optional expr is not LL(1); the independent grammar must settle this rather than omit value alternatives. Approval must include a mechanical check, not just the algorithm description.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:643:17. **OPEN-17 — Exact kept pattern/arm surface (9/10/16).** Recommend qualified enum patterns, `_` catch-all, integer/bool/char literals, OR patterns, named field renaming, whole-payload `{..}` and a mandatory comma after every arm. Keep irrefutable enum lets, mut applying to every binder, explicit field handling and the deferred status of nested patterns. Alternative: comma only after non-block arms, subject to FIRST/FOLLOW proof. Clarify OD25’s “bare” fieldless wording against the chapter’s qualification rule; explicitly disposition generic `E::<T>::V` and module-qualified let paths. Do not treat the frozen parser as authority for a new accepted form.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:647:21. **OPEN-21 — API/view spellings and branded signatures (7/15/16/19/21–27).** Recommend View/ViewMut second-class parameter constructors and ordinary calls for the decided ct_select/ct_eq/text/container APIs; use exact explicit branded type arguments; floating conversions use `name::<Target>(x)`. Alternative: &[]-style view types and qualified associated APIs. Reason: feature names in Q3/Q4 and the information-flow decision do not decide every arity, type position, qualifier or conversion target syntax. Submit the exhaustive concrete signature table before encoding it; no fabricated complete signatures here.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:649:23. **OPEN-23 — Remaining raw/FFI API closure (24/25).** Preserve decided `kept buf: H` for an owned allocation, unmarked call-only parameters, paired `Kept<H>` completion, and the absolute ban on borrow-derived kept arguments (full Q3.12). Recommend ptr-qualified raw APIs except decided `read_owned(p)`, and extern fn without ABI-string blocks. Alternative for the remaining qualification choice: global raw operation names. Marker placement/default and receipt signatures are transcription obligations, not open alternatives.
