docs/decisions.md:182:- **The generated-chapter requirement** (rows Q9.15, P3): Lean is the specification, in one main normative file with doc comments and examples; no prose is generated from it. This confirms the [2026-11-04 decision](#decided-project-lean-is-the-spec). The "one main normative file" wording is revised 2026-11-06 by the [long-term changes](#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06): one authoritative specification library in cohesive modules, with `ConcreteSpec/Spec.lean` as its public import.
docs/decisions.md:186:- <a id="decided-2026-11-05-q9-1-reads"></a>**Q9.1, read forms** (owner-confirmed, 2026-11-05): `copy x` is allowed only when `x` has a Copy type and `move x` only when it has a non-Copy (linear) type. Each read has one form; `move` of a Copy value and `copy` of a linear value are both refused.
docs/decisions.md:254:- **Q8.1** What is the first proof endpoint? — Proved source→BIR; qualified native; conditional image claim.
docs/decisions.md:257:- **Q8.4** Does the first artifact qualify as a complete executable? — Component plus bound launcher first.
docs/decisions.md:260:- **Q8.7** What prevents vacuous correctness? — Coverage, realizable witnesses and rejection controls; a spec where every allocation fails fails qualification.
docs/decisions.md:283:- **P1** Where agent discretion ends — Claude and Codex reason every question from the philosophy and recommend; they never pick a language answer through code, fixtures, diagnostics or docs. 'Important' = anything that revises a decided rule, changes observable language meaning you have not ruled on, or that you reserved. Every important decision comes to you.
